    board: GitReins verdict history — the audit trail for this tick's judged rows
    
    The fleet convention is that verdict.json lands under .gitreins/history/ and is
    tracked (crier, hermes-dagger et al. commit theirs); without that the judge's
    evidence lives only on this host. These are the verdicts from judging AUG-006,
    AUG-007 and GITREINS-JUDGE, including the two that FAILED:
    
      * AUG-006 tier-1 FAIL at a2ef761 — the row's own defect (429 reaching cmd_init
        -> crash -> leaked namespace). Kept, not squashed: it is the evidence that
        motivated d2dcad3, and a history that only holds passes cannot show why a fix
        was needed.
      * AUG-006 tier-2 INCOMPLETE ("Committed HEAD d2dcad3 is FLAKY, not reliably
        green") — the judge independently found the concurrency flake that 9f6d9c9
        fixed. Strongest single piece of evidence in this tick: an automated grader
        reproduced the defect the suite had been hiding.
      * GITREINS-JUDGE FAIL at d2dcad3 — its tests arm hit the same unscoped leak
        audit, i.e. the config row failed for a defect that was not its own; closed
        separately with that stated.
    
    Tier-2 re-judges for AUG-006 and AUG-007 were dispatched at the fixed tip
    9f6d9c9; their verdicts land in a later tick's commit, and this commit must not
    be read as claiming them.
