++{"attempts":0,"blocked_reason":null,"blocked_since":null,"blocks":[],"capability_tags":["bundle","engine","gate","spec-002"],"ci_result":null,"commit_hash":null,"completed_at":null,"complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-09-20T23:39:09.391009+00:00","depends_on":[],"dispatched_at":null,"exit_code":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":null,"guard_result":null,"id":"AUG-010","lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"perpetual":null,"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"priority":"P1","reasoning":"docs/SPEC-002-bundles.md sections 2.1 and 2.2. The two behaviours that make bundling worth having. (a) GATE searches EVERY member's namespace: evidence = recall_many([ns(m) for m in bundle_members(p)], q) - this is cross-project decision dedupe, so if terminal-jail already decided how a sandbox isolates the filesystem, bunker LINKS that answer instead of re-deciding it and drifting; the satisfies edge gains src_project so the reader sees it came from a sibling. (b) IMPACT crosses the boundary for bundle-scoped decisions only: a project-local decision never crosses (or every answer reaches every project and the pass is quadratic again), and a breaks edge INTO A SIBLING IS AN ESCALATION, NOT A SILENT CHANGE - the engine records the break and surfaces it, it never rewrites another project's spec. Depth triage for a bundle-scoped decision takes the MAX blast radius across members. Acceptance: a question already answered in a sibling namespace is LINKED not asked; a bundle-scoped answer that invalidates a sibling decision produces a breaks edge naming that sibling and an escalation row; a project-scoped answer produces NO cross-project edge.","review_notes":null,"status":"pending","title":"[P1] bundle-aware GATE and cross-boundary IMPACT — SPEC-002 2.1/2.2","updated_at":"2026-09-20T23:39:09.391009+00:00","worker_status":"pending","worker_summary":null,"detail":{"fingerprint":"283676204b1d0d22ad891821c7718a6ff3e8b02e4b5f5898fca7f2931ec5